# BACKEND .env — DEPRECATED. Please use the SINGLE ROOT ../.env file instead.
#
# All env vars for the whole project live in the repo root:
#     facial/
#       .env              <-- EDIT THIS ONE (copy from ../.env.example)
#       backend/
#         .env.example    <-- this file (info only)
#
# Variables required by the backend (see ../.env.example for full docs):
#   DATABASE_URL        PostgreSQL/Supabase connection string
#   API_TITLE, API_VERSION  (optional metadata)
#   HOST, PORT, DEBUG  (local dev; Render overrides PORT)
#   CORS_ORIGINS       Comma-separated allowed frontend URLs
#   EDGE_API_KEY       Shared secret matching the edge node env
#
# Why still works: backend/config.py walks UP to ../.env automatically.
# No need to duplicate anything here.
